  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Last year Mr. John Q. Public received an inheritance. He paid \\(20\\%\\) in federal taxes on the inheritance, and paid \\(10\\%\\) of what he had left in state taxes. He paid a total of \\(\\$10{,}500\\) for both taxes. How many dollars was the inheritance?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(30{,}000\\)",
    "B": "\\(32{,}500\\)",
    "C": "\\(35{,}000\\)",
    "D": "\\(37{,}500\\)",
    "E": "\\(40{,}000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "After paying the federal tax, Mr. Public had \\(100\\%-20\\%=80\\%\\) of the inheritance left. The state tax was \\(10\\%\\) of that remaining amount, so it was\n\\[\n0.10\\cdot0.80=0.08=8\\%\n\\]\nof the original inheritance. Together, the taxes were \\(20\\%+8\\%=28\\%\\) of the inheritance.\n\nSince this \\(28\\%\\) amounted to \\(\\$10{,}500\\), the whole inheritance was\n\\[\n10{,}500\\div0.28=37{,}500.\n\\]\nIndeed, the federal tax was \\(\\$7{,}500\\), leaving \\(\\$30{,}000\\); the state tax was then \\(\\$3{,}000\\), giving the required total tax. The inheritance was \\(\\boxed{\\$37{,}500}\\), choice D.",
